# Frontend Optimization — Client/Server Boundary Refactor

**Branch:** V3-Frontend
**Approach:** Option A — keep data fetching client-side, server-render the static
chrome; push `"use client"` down to the smallest interactive leaves. No backend
changes, auth untouched.
**Scope:** Boundary refactor + dead-code removal only. Asset perf (next/image,
woff2 fonts) intentionally out of scope. Loading-state UX may be improved.

## Why not full SSR of data
Auth is cookie-based against a separate backend origin (`NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`).
That cookie is scoped to the backend's domain, so the Next.js server can't read
it and can't fetch user data server-side without proxying the API (a backend
re-architecture we explicitly deferred). So data stays client-fetched; only the
static frame moves to the server.

